spec.section:
### 1.1 Schema versioning and evolution

The existing `contracts/config.schema.json` is schema **v2**
(`schema_version: { const: 2 }`). This volume defines **v4** as a strict
superset delta (v3 added the hierarchy/capability/composition blocks; v4 adds
sessions, storage, admission, worker, capacity and measurement). The full v3 file is the contracts task's deliverable; the
delta below is normative for it.

- **VOLD-001** — `schema_version` is a monotonically increasing integer.
  A loader MUST refuse any version it does not implement with error
  `schema_version_unsupported` (naming the highest supported version) and
  MUST NOT auto-migrate silently. Migration v2→v3 is additive: every v2
  document is a valid v4 document unchanged (all v3 additions are optional
  at parse level but some become REQUIRED by the rules of §1.3 — see
  VOLD-003). Migration code, if any, prints the field-by-field diff it
  applied.
- **VOLD-002** — `additionalProperties: false` is retained at every level.
  An unknown field is a load error `unknown_field{path}`, never a warning:
  typo'd capability or grant names must fail closed (F-005 "invalid
  configuration examples produce specified outcomes").

**v3/v4 `$defs` additions (delta to config.schema.json):**

```json
"hierarchy": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["manager_creation"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "manager_creation": { "$ref": "#/$defs/managerCreation" }
  }
},
"managerCreation": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["enabled", "max_director_created", "provisioning"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "enabled": { "type": "boolean" },
    "max_director_created": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
    "provisioning": { "$ref": "#/$defs/managerProvisioning" }
  }
},
"managerProvisioning": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["role_template", "gateway_pool", "token_provisioning"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "role_template": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "gateway_pool": { "type": "array", "minItems": 1,
      "items": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^gw-[a-z0-9-]+$" } },
    "token_provisioning": { "const": "operator" }
  }
},
"capability": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["grants", "grantable_pool", "create_subordinate"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "grants": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/$defs/grant" } },
    "grantable_pool": { "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 } },
    "create_subordinate": { "enum": ["none", "supervisor", "manager"] }
  }
},
"grant": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["tool", "scope", "origin"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "tool": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "scope": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "origin": { "enum": ["vp", "director"] },
    "granted_by": { "type": "string" },
    "granted_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
    "expires_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
    "revoked": { "type": "boolean", "default": false }
  }
},
"approval": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["human_approval_required", "gates"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "human_approval_required": { "type": "boolean" },
    "gates": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 } }
  }
},
"hermesBinding": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["instance", "profile"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "instance": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^gw-[a-z0-9-]+$" },
    "profile": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$" }
  }
},
"runtime": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["provider", "model", "context_window"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "provider": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "model": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "context_window": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
    "max_turns": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
    "token_budget": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 }
  }
},
"composition": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["base_role", "specialization"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "base_role": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "specialization": { "$ref": "#/$defs/specialization" },
    "project_scope": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^/" } }
  }
},
"specialization": {
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["name", "authorized_overrides"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "name": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "authorized_overrides": { "type": "array",
      "items": { "enum": ["behavior", "permissions"] } }
  }
}
```

Notes on the delta:
- `capability.grants` generalizes the existing flat `tools.include/exclude`:
  include/exclude remain the *ruleset* passed into the session
  configuration (DESIGN §3.6); `grants` is the *authorization record* with
  provenance. A tool in `tools.include` without a matching grant of origin
  `vp` or `director` fails validation `tool_without_grant` — skill wording
  or skill-list membership alone is never an effective permission (F-012
  rule, enforced here at load time).
- `hermesBinding` is additive to, not a replacement of, `agent.gateway`:
  `gateway` remains the transport/concurrency binding; `hermesBinding`
  names which Hermes instance (a gateway id) and which named profile on it
  the agent's sessions run under.

### 2.4 Provisioning sequence (cards live in contracts/OPERATIONS.md)

- **VOLD-072.** The canonical sequence for adding any role is:
  1. operator writes the desired config (schema-valid, `profile` distinct);
  2. credentials are provisioned for that profile (operator action — never
     automated by an agent);
  3. the profile is created on the target gateway;
  4. assets/skills are uploaded and verified;
  5. readiness gates pass (§5.1, plus a profile-readiness probe: the gateway can
     run a turn under that profile and the effective config matches);
  6. the agent is registered (`/chd/registry/<agent>`), its rooms are opened, its
     bond is provisioned at first wake;
  7. a smoke turn is recorded as evidence (one real wake, one report).
  A failure at any step leaves the agent **not dispatchable** and names the failed
  step; there is no "partially ready" state.
- **VOLD-073.** Migration of an existing default-profile agent: create the new
  profile, converge config and assets, verify readiness, switch the binding, then
  retire the default-profile binding. The agent's existing sessions are archived
  before the switch (VOL-F); no session id is reused across profiles.

### 7.11 Figure CHD-F03 — Crier federation (new)

Class: architecture + sequence. This figure is a federation swimlane, not a
room-delivery ACK diagram. Name every actor and arrow:

- **Lanes/actors:** OWNER A / VP-A → DIRECTOR-A → MANAGERS/SUPERVISORS /
  FOREMEN/WORKERS-A; CRIER PEER LINK; OWNER B / VP-B → LOCAL TRUST + APPROVAL
  POLICY-B → DIRECTOR-B → MANAGERS/SUPERVISORS / FOREMEN/WORKERS-B; AUDIT STORE-B.
  Add a second peer-director lane for `DIRECTOR-C` to show one owner coordinating
  several client directors, and mark that example illustrative, not universal.
- **Arrows:** DIRECTOR-A → CRIER `REQUEST pr-42 [peer identity + scope]`;
  CRIER → TRUST POLICY-B `AUTHENTICATE + MAP ACTOR peer:client-alpha`;
  TRUST POLICY-B → VP-B `APPROVAL REQUEST [scope/owner decision]`;
  VP-B → POLICY-B `APPROVE or DENY`;
  POLICY-B → DIRECTOR-B `PERMIT objective/ticket OR HOLD/DENY`;
  DIRECTOR-B → MANAGERS-B `ASSIGN permitted work`;
  WORKERS-B → DIRECTOR-B `REPORT rr-42 [ticket + digest]`;
  DIRECTOR-B → CRIER `CORRELATED REPORT rr-42 [pr-42]`;
  CRIER → DIRECTOR-A `REPLY/REPORT [pr-42, dedupe]`;
  POLICY-B → AUDIT STORE-B `ACCEPT/DENY/GRANT/PROVENANCE AUDIT`;
  CRIER → DIRECTOR-B `RETRY duplicate [same pr-42]` (no second objective).
  Draw an explicit POLICY-B → CRIER `DENY 403 peer_scope_denied` and
  `HOLD 202 pending_local_approval` path.
- **Callouts:** `LOCAL VP PRECEDENCE`; `CONNECTIVITY OR SENDER ID NEVER GRANTS
  VP`; `peer trust ≠ VP grant`; `OUTAGE ISOLATES FEDERATION, LOCAL WORK CONTINUES`.
  Show the local-only reinvocation path DIRECTOR-B → DIRECTOR-B as a separate
  dashed edge labeled `INTERNAL REINVOCATION (NOT AUTONOMOUS PEER)`.

Trace: VOLD-088, VOLC §8.2/§8.3. The owner-A/owner-B and one-owner/many-client
examples are illustrative topologies, not a universal deployment shape.
